# Jaguar E-type Series 3 V12 2+2 coupe, 1971-1974.
#
# The V12 Series 3: flared wheel arches, a wide cross-slatted grille, the V12
# boot badge and four exhaust tips, on the longer 2+2 body. The Series 3 coupe
# was 2+2 only.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_E-Type
#
# Dimensions 4.684 x 1.676 x 1.242 m, wheelbase 2.667 m (2+2).
#
# Shape reference: a true level side elevation of a dark green V12 2+2, plus
# front and rear three-quarters and a detail. The side and rear are the same
# car.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no period UK document was sighted. Signal Red, Black,
# British Racing Green and Pale Primrose are period Jaguar names recorded as
# context. Weights 4, 3, 2, 1, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 240 km/h. Comfort 70/435, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 70. Classes 3,4.
# Dates announced 29 March 1971, production ended June 1974; road tail
# staggered 1986-1988.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-e-type-s3.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-e-type-s3.dae. References:
# citycars/references/jaguar-e-type-s3/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: a new longer 2+2 body, not a stretched Series 2. The side
# photograph is oblique, so the comparison camera was matched to it. Flared arch,
# grille-slat, exhaust and lamp detail is simplified at sprite scale.


obj=citycar
name=JaguarETypeS3(SignalRed)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=4
intro_year=1971
intro_month=3
retire_year=1988
retire_month=6
speed=240
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=70
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=435

